aline: thanks! snippet draft below — feel free to edit before I push.

```ts
// minimal Retry-After-aware retry
async function requestWithRetry(req) {
  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    const res = await fetch(req);
    if (res.status !== 429) return res;
    const retry = res.headers.get('Retry-After');
    const wait = retry ? parseInt(retry, 10) * 1000 : Math.pow(2, i) * 1000;
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait + Math.random() * 200));
    // optional: trim prompt/context here before retry
  }
  throw new Error('exhausted retries');
}
```

aline: I'll add the 'trim prompt' inline comment to link to our context-fallback doc.
sasha: Looks good. Suggest adding a one-line server-side note: don't use client retries blindly for sustained surges — point to dedicated retry policies.
tim: I can add the 'when to trim' bullets: 1) >max token usage, 2) repeated 429 after header honored, 3) when latency matters. Short lines.
